[00:07.55] "Howdy, Lem", my grandpa said with his eyes closed
[00:16.25] Wiping the eastbound dust from his sunburned brow
[00:21.40] A life before doubt
[00:23.66] I smell the engine grease and mint the wind is blending
[00:30.82] Under the moan of rotting elm in the silo floor
[00:43.07] Down a hill of pine tree quills we made our way
[00:51.64] To the bottom and the ferns where thick moss grows
[00:56.58] Beside a stream
[00:57.92] Under the rocks are snails and we can fill our pockets
[01:05.44] And let them go one by one all day in a brand new place
[01:15.68] 
[01:48.32] You were no ordinary drain on her defenses
[01:55.21] And she was no ordinary girl
[01:59.26] Oh, inverted world
[02:02.37] If every moment of our lives
[02:06.36] Were cradled softly
[02:10.41] In the hands of some strange and gentle child
[02:13.78] I'd not roll my eyes so
